# BNDZ Terminal Quality Gates

Apply on **every** Open Terminal / Local terminal change on BNDZShell.

## Locked architecture (2026-09-19)

- Local PowerShell on BNDZShell = **WinUI `EasyTerminalControl`** in `NativeTerminalHost`, overlaid on the Remote plugin hole via `NATIVE_TERMINAL_OPEN` / `LAYOUT` / `CLOSE`.
- React supplies the hole rect only (`NativeTerminalHole`). **No xterm.js Local paint path on BNDZShell.**
- SSH on BNDZShell may use TermControl with an `ssh …` startup command line (same host).

## Gates (G0–G5)

See `docs/TERMINAL-QUALITY-GATES.md`. Before claiming terminal ready:

1. Run `scripts/verify-terminal-gates.ps1`
2. Fresh `npm run build` + native Debug build (G5)
3. Do **not** silently pivot Local back to ConPTY→xterm-in-WebView without updating `docs/TERMINAL-QUALITY-GATES.md` + `docs/LAUNCH-READY-PLAN.md` **and** telling the user in the same turn

## MUST NOT

- Claim Local works via xterm-in-Remote on BNDZShell
- Refuse `NATIVE_TERMINAL_OPEN` as “retired” while this rule is active
- Leave EasyTerminalControl package unreferenced

```text
❌ BAD: meshTerminalOpen({ local: true }) → xterm blank pane on BNDZShell
✅ GOOD: nativeTerminalOpen → EasyTerminalControl overlay → real PS prompt
```
